    "solution": {
      "en": "Daniel developed recurrent drug-induced hypoglycemia after taking an unregulated slimming capsule adulterated with a sulfonylurea. Low glucose coincided with symptoms and correction relieved them. Insulin and C-peptide were inappropriately present during the low; this does not alone separate an insulinoma from a secretagogue. The positive drug screen and independently tested capsule supply that distinction. Skipped meals increased vulnerability but do not explain the drug result. The team stops the product and arranges monitored clinical care.",
      "id": "Daniel mengalami hipoglikemia berulang akibat kapsul pelangsing tidak teregulasi yang dicampur sulfonilurea. Glukosa rendah bertepatan dengan gejala, dan koreksinya meredakan gejala. Insulin serta C-peptida tidak tersupresi saat glukosa rendah; temuan ini saja tidak membedakan insulinoma dari obat pemicu sekresi insulin. Skrining obat positif dan pengujian kapsul secara independen memberi pembeda itu. Melewatkan makan meningkatkan kerentanan, tetapi tidak menjelaskan hasil obat. Tim menghentikan produk dan menyiapkan perawatan dengan pemantauan."
    },
