    "solution": {
      "en": "Felix Orne altered identity mappings in final forensic exports to protect selected aliases from the service exposed in The Ghostmaker. Retained extracts and an independent laboratory reject the substituted associations; the external revision journal attributes them to his privileged sessions. Rebecca recognized that pattern and preserved the source material. Felix killed her during the documented archive encounter and staged selective burglary to recover her copies. Continuous access footage, her preserved confrontation recording, the recovered blood-bearing damaged blade and its physical fracture fit independently support the murder allegation. Analytical uncertainty in Ed’s original annotations is genuine but does not explain the later identity replacements. Certified alias records and matched settlement payments link the forensic service to the identity and finance divisions. They establish institutional protection, not proof that any one division head controlled all the others.",
      "id": "Felix Orne mengubah pemetaan identitas pada ekspor forensik akhir untuk melindungi alias tertentu dari layanan yang diungkap The Ghostmaker. Ekstrak disimpan serta laboratorium independen menolak hubungan disubstitusi; jurnal revisi luar mengaitkannya dengan sesi berhak istimewanya. Rebecca mengenali pola serta menyimpan material sumber. Felix membunuhnya saat pertemuan arsip terdokumentasi lalu merekayasa pencurian selektif untuk merebut salinannya. Rekaman akses tanpa jeda, rekaman konfrontasi tersimpan, bilah rusak berdarah ditemukan, serta kecocokan patahan fisik mendukung tuduhan pembunuhan secara independen. Ketidakpastian analitis pada anotasi asli Ed nyata tetapi tidak menjelaskan penggantian identitas belakangan. Catatan alias tersertifikasi serta pembayaran penyelesaian cocok menghubungkan layanan forensik dengan divisi identitas serta keuangan. Ini memastikan perlindungan institusional, bukan bukti satu kepala divisi mengendalikan semua lainnya."
    },
